>:<fpage>E145</fpage>&#x02013;E147.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11389456</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Reits, E.A., A.M. Benham, B. Plougastel, J. Neefjes, and J. Trowsdale. <year>1997</year>. Dynamics of proteasome distribution in living cells. <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>16</volume>:<fpage>6087</fpage>&#x02013;6094.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9321388</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Talcott, B., and M.S. Moore. <year>1999</year>. Getting across the nuclear pore complex. <source>Trends Cell Biol.</source> <volume>9</volume>:<fpage>312</fpage>&#x02013;318.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10407410</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">van Ham, S.M., E.P. Tjin, B.F. Lillemeier, U. Gruneberg, K.E. van Meijgaarden, L. Pastoors, D. Verwoerd, A. Tulp, B. Canas, D. Rahman, et al. <year>1997</year>. HLA-DO is a negative modulator of HLA-DM-mediated MHC class II peptide loading. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>7</volume>:<fpage>950</fpage>&#x02013;957.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9382849</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Varshavsky, A. <year>2005</year>. Regulated protein degradation. <source>Trends Biochem. Sci.</source> <volume>30</volume>:<fpage>283</fpage>&#x02013;286.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15950869</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Wang, H., L. Wang, H. Erdjument-Bromage, M. Vidal, P. Tempst, R.S. Jones, and Y. Zhang. <year>2004</year>. Role of histone H2A ubiquitination in Polycomb silencing. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>431</volume>:<fpage>873</fpage>&#x02013;878.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15386022</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>